<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Entitlements baked into the main binary BEFORE packaging.

	  Why this file must exist and must NOT contain get-task-allow:
	  TrollStore RootHelper signApp() dumps the existing entitlements from the
	  main executable. If the executable has NONE, it injects a fallback dict
	  that includes get-task-allow=true. On iOS 16+, any binary carrying
	  get-task-allow requires Developer Mode to be enabled, otherwise the
	  process is killed on launch (instant crash / no icon refresh).

	  By pre-signing with this non-empty dict we keep application-identifier
	  (normal app behaviour) while dodging both the fallback injection and the
	  Developer Mode requirement.

	  Never add here:
	    get-task-allow, task_for_pid-allow, com.apple.system-task-ports*,
	    com.apple.private.cs.debugger            -> forces Developer Mode
	    dynamic-codesigning,
	    com.apple.private.skip-library-validation -> banned on iOS 15/A12+

	  CarPlay (audio app):
	    com.apple.developer.carplay-audio is required for the system to grant
	    a CPTemplateApplicationScene. It is normally a protected entitlement
	    needing a provisioning profile; TrollStore/CoreTrust does not validate
	    entitlement legitimacy. Phase 0 probe exists to verify whether carplayd
	    performs a secondary check on iOS 16.1.1. If the CarPlay screen does
	    not appear, this path is blocked and a real signing route is needed.

	  application-identifier / keychain-access-groups were updated from the
	  legacy `app.musicfree.trollstore` to the actual bundle identifier
	  `app.musicfree.ios` (system services are sensitive to mismatch).
	-->
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>app.musicfree.ios</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
	<string>TROLLTROLL</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.carplay-audio</key>
	<true/>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>app.musicfree.ios</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
